1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,030
What if someone is following
you down a dark alley?

2
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:05,570
Imagine walking
home late at night.

3
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:07,290
The streets are almost empty.

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:09,130
There are barely any cars,

5
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:12,110
and the only sound you can
hear is your own footsteps.

6
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,050
But then, you notice
something strange.

7
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,090
Someone is walking behind you.

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,550
You turn right.

9
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:19,870
He turns right.

10
00:00:20,140 --> 00:00:21,570
You cross the street.

11
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,590
He crosses the street too.

12
00:00:23,820 --> 00:00:25,860
You stop in front
of a shop window,

13
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,310
pretending to
look at something.

14
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:29,970
And in the reflection,
you see him.

15
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,470
A tall man wearing
a black jacket.

16
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:35,310
He is standing just a
few meters behind you.

17
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:37,790
And he is looking
directly at you.

18
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,810
You tell yourself it's
probably just a coincidence.

19
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,110
But then he starts
getting closer.

20
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,790
And when you take out your
phone to call someone,

21
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:47,450
he takes out his too.

22
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:50,830
But this story actually
started 20 minutes earlier.

23
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:53,170
You were walking home
after meeting a friend.

24
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:54,600
It was already late,

25
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,400
and there were
almost no buses left.

26
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:58,450
So you decided to walk.

27
00:00:58,720 --> 00:01:00,330
You knew this
neighborhood well.

28
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:02,950
You had walked these
streets hundreds of times.

29
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:04,990
Nothing had ever
happened before.

30
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,790
At first, you heard ordinary
footsteps behind you.

31
00:01:08,820 --> 00:01:10,390
You didn't think much of it.

32
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:13,090
But after a few minutes,
you realize something.

33
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:15,450
The footsteps
never disappeared.

34
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,270
You walked faster.

35
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:19,170
He walked faster too.

36
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:22,110
You stopped near a shop
and checked your phone.

37
00:01:22,480 --> 00:01:24,060
Through the reflection
in the window,

38
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,020
you saw him again.

39
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:27,790
He was standing
about 10 meters away.

40
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:31,370
Now you were sure someone
was following you.

41
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:33,570
You decided to take
a different route.

42
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,730
You turned into
a narrow alley,

43
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:37,890
hoping he would continue
down the main street.

44
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,210
But a few seconds later, you
heard the same footsteps.

45
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:42,950
He had followed you.

46
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,550
The alley was much darker
than you remembered.

47
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:48,050
Old garages stood on one side.

48
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,270
Tall apartment walls
stood on the other.

49
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:52,810
The streetlights barely
reached the ground.

50
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:54,080
You took out your phone.

51
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,030
You wanted to
call your friend.

52
00:01:56,260 --> 00:01:58,200
But before you could
press the call button,

53
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,390
you heard a voice.

54
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,810
"Hey, wait."

55
00:02:01,380 --> 00:02:02,610
You didn't turn around.

56
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:04,290
"I'm talking to you."

57
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,670
The voice was much closer now.

58
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,510
You started walking faster.

59
00:02:08,820 --> 00:02:10,510
The exit was just ahead.

60
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:13,130
You could already see the
lights of the main street.

61
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,130
Then your phone vibrated.

62
00:02:15,380 --> 00:02:17,590
A message appeared
from an unknown number.

63
00:02:17,620 --> 00:02:21,210
It said: "Don't
turn around. Run."

64
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,830
You froze.

65
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:24,590
Who sent that message?

66
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,670
And how did they know
what was happening?

67
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,930
You slowly turned around.

68
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:31,950
The man was standing
only a few steps away.

69
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:35,690
He was tall, broad-shouldered,
and wearing a black jacket.

70
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:38,130
His face was hidden
in the darkness.

71
00:02:38,820 --> 00:02:41,290
"Finally stopped,"
he said quietly.

72
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,130
You asked him what he wanted.

73
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,510
He didn't answer.

74
00:02:44,820 --> 00:02:48,030
Instead, he took out his phone
and showed you the screen.

75
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,010
There was a photograph of you.

76
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:52,090
It had been taken
earlier that evening.

77
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:54,140
You were standing
right outside the shop

78
00:02:54,160 --> 00:02:55,910
where you had
first noticed him.

79
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:57,480
"Where did you get that?"

80
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:58,500
You asked.

81
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:00,810
The man slowly put
his phone away.

82
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,290
"You'd better stop
asking questions."

83
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:06,350
Suddenly, you noticed
movement near the exit.

84
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,570
Another person was
standing there.

85
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:09,790
He wasn't moving.

86
00:03:09,940 --> 00:03:11,530
He was just watching you.

87
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:14,060
Now there were two
strangers between you

88
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:15,230
and the main street.

89
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:16,910
You stepped backward.

90
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,090
The first man stepped forward.

91
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:23,330
Then, suddenly, a loud noise
came from somewhere behind him.

92
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,850
A door slammed.

93
00:03:25,260 --> 00:03:27,720
For a moment, headlights
from a passing car

94
00:03:27,740 --> 00:03:29,370
lit up the entire alley.

95
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:32,570
You used that moment to move
toward the brighter street.

96
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:34,770
The strangers didn't grab you.

97
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,150
They simply watched
as you walked away.

98
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,560
When you finally
reached the main road,

99
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,950
you saw a 24-hour
convenience store.

100
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:43,890
There was a shopkeeper inside.

101
00:03:44,240 --> 00:03:46,120
Next to it was a
guarded parking lot

102
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:48,690
with a security guard
standing near the entrance.

103
00:03:49,140 --> 00:03:51,650
You quickly took out your
phone to call for help.

104
00:03:51,820 --> 00:03:54,770
But before you could dial,
another message appeared.

105
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:57,350
"You chose the wrong place."

106
00:03:57,880 --> 00:03:59,090
You looked up.

107
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:02,530
Across the street stood the
same man in the black jacket.

108
00:04:02,840 --> 00:04:03,840
He smiled.

109
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,230
Then he slowly
raised his phone.

110
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:09,350
On the screen was another
photograph of you.

111
00:04:09,440 --> 00:04:11,640
But this time, someone
else was standing

112
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:12,950
right next to you.

113
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,140
You looked around.

114
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:15,990
There was nobody there.

115
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:18,310
And that's when you
realize something.

116
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,640
Maybe the danger
had been much closer

117
00:04:20,660 --> 00:04:22,170
than you ever imagined.

118
00:04:22,860 --> 00:04:24,690
Now, you have two choices.

119
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:27,610
Option A, enter the
convenience store,

120
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:29,310
tell the shopkeeper
what happened,

121
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,110
and ask them to
call the police.

122
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,600
Option B, go to the
guarded parking lot

123
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:36,870
and ask the security
guard for help.

124
00:04:37,440 --> 00:04:38,710
What would you choose?

125
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:40,920
Comment A or B below.

126
00:04:40,940 --> 00:04:44,670
Your choice will decide what
happens in the next episode.

